Chapter 10: The Land of the Lion King

Chapter 10.39: "Let's Do This Together"

---

It didn't feel as though it had been a long time since Subaru had last experienced 『Door Crossing』, to the point where he might even feel nostalgic.

Originally, this spatial transportation through a door hardly gave one any sense of having crossed through space at all. Just as when entering or leaving an ordinary room, all that happened was that one's footsteps crossed the threshold connecting two spaces.

And so, the reason Subaru couldn't help letting out a breath at that moment wasn't because of any particular sentiment toward 『Door Crossing』, but rather his reaction to looking around the room he'd been brought into.

"This is... Certainly a mysterious room that a witch would love."

It was a room with an unusual structure, its entire circumference lined with windows along the walls. It was spacious, and presumably located at the very top of the castle. The blue sky stretching beyond the windows, along with the white clouds drifting beneath it, gave him a vague idea of the room's position.

The scenery outside wasn't the endless, bottomless otherworldly space that was still fresh in Subaru's memories, but the sky of the surface world itself.

In other words, this was proof that what Tīga had told them wasn't a lie.

"The floating castle, Kugelschreiber, huh...? Getting an airship makes it feel like you're finally entering the endgame of an RPG, doesn't it? Don't you get that feeling?"

"I have no idea what you're talking about, but it sounds unimportant. More importantly, look."

"—Subaru!"

After responding coldly to Subaru's admiration, Ferris pointed straight ahead. From the far end of the room, Beatrice came running toward them, her dress fluttering.

As she leaped at him from directly in front, Subaru, who was carrying Crusch on his back, caught her against his chest. Somehow managing to keep his balance, he was relieved to see that she appeared unharmed at a glance.

"Beako, I'm glad you're safe. What a relief."

"That's Betty's line, I suppose! We got separated like that, and then you ran off without listening to Betty's voice! I was terribly worried!"

"That wasn't my fault. It was because of the enemy's dirty tricks... Anyway, somehow, everyone on our side made it out safely. Did anything happen on your end...? Well, something obviously did."

"Indeed. —I moved the castle."

With both hands on her hips, Beatrice nodded with a triumphant expression.

Her proud demeanor was adorable, but as far as Subaru was concerned, the connection between their situation until just a moment ago and the decision to move the castle was a mystery.

And so, despite the romantic appeal of a flying castle, he had plenty of questions about that decision—.

"After consulting with the 『Librarian』, moving the castle was my decision. The entrance we had used to come and go was under the enemy's control, and there was a possibility they were lying in wait for us."

Instead of Beatrice, it was Russell, standing in the middle of the room, who answered Subaru's question.

In the center of the spacious room stood a circular platform large enough for several adults to surround. Above it floated a strange black sphere, and Russell had his hand extended toward it.

It was some sort of fantastical device, but apparently, he couldn't move away from it. Subaru and the others therefore walked over to him.

"Is that... a map of the world carved into the platform?"

"Yes, it appears to be more or less that. However, because the map was carved quite some time ago, there are many differences from the current map of the world. It doesn't cause us much inconvenience, though."

Peering down at the circular platform, Subaru saw a map of the world carved into its surface, with the terrain represented through raised and lowered sections.

Just as Russell had said, it appeared to depict an era much older than the present.

Considering Kugelschreiber Castle's history, it was probably a map from more than four hundred years ago. Subaru felt a growing desire to bring out a modern map of the world and compare the two, but—

"Let's leave that for later... Mr. Russell, what do you mean by lying in wait?"

"Call me the 『Silver Fox』. —It was an obvious deduction. In my eyes, the value of the teleportation route had dropped considerably, and there were 『Beloved Children』 who had infiltrated the castle... It would be unreasonable to assume that the enemy's numbers were small."

"Maybe some bastard who was impatient to claim the credit was trying to make a move on his own. There're always guys who can't get along with everyone else, no matter where you go. Especially when it comes to those 『Beloved Children』. None of them seem to have any sense of camaraderie."

Following Russell's answer, Rachins glanced at Melty and 『Black Hound』 beside him.

It was true that the two had formerly been 『Beloved Children』, but Subaru wanted to defend them against that unfair assessment. Though, when it came to 『Black Hound』, it was difficult to argue that he had much of a sense of camaraderie.

"Even so, thanks to the bonds we've forged over these past two months, we managed to drive the enemy back. Right, 『Black Hound』?"

"Bonds? Hey, hey, don't say something so disgusting it makes me sick! It's purely by chance, a miraculous coincidence! The only thing we have in common is that we hate the same bastards, riiight?"

"See? We're getting along just fine. It's just that there are a lot of people who don't understand how to communicate."

With both thumbs pointed downward in a thumbs-down gesture, 『Black Hound』 responded.

Subaru shrugged. Rachins seemed to have some objections to Subaru's interpretation, but perhaps he couldn't see any point in arguing about it, because he simply concluded, "Well, whatever," and continued.

"Anyway, that's why we moved around to avoid the ambush and met up with the 『Librarian』. This guy wanted to go looking for you lot, but..."

"After explaining the circumstances, we discussed an alternative plan. We concluded that if we disrupted the enemy's position and forced them to abandon their ambush, they would have no choice but to change their approach—"

"Betty moved Mother's castle, I suppose."

With that, the thought process of the people who had been acting separately was finally laid out, and Subaru was able to understand.

All that remained was figuring out how they had actually managed to move the castle in order to put that conclusion into practice—.

"Does that black sphere the 『Silver Fox』 has been holding his hand over have something to do with it?"

"Yes. The precise mechanism is unknown, but the castle appears to move in response to the operator's will. Though, without the 『Librarian』, I doubt we would have discovered how to activate it."

"I see. Good job, good job. You're the savior of all our lives."

"Of course I am. ...But it was nerve-racking not being able to stay by your side, I suppose."

Beatrice lightly pinched the hem of Subaru's clothes and looked up at him with lowered eyes.

Her expression was so endearing. Even if Beatrice had accepted the plan as a way to break through their predicament, putting off rushing to Subaru's side after they'd been separated must have taken considerable courage.

Subaru was glad that her brave decision hadn't gone to waste.

"Um, I understand the situation now. But is it really okay to make the castle fly? Won't it stand out too much and cause us to be pursued constantly...?"

"Of course, we've already discussed that point. 『Librarian』, this castle has—"

"It has an effect that 『Obstructs Recognition』. It's not as though we're going to keep parading flamboyantly through the sky forever, I suppose. However, we shouldn't be overconfident, since particularly perceptive people, or those who've been inside the castle before, might be able to see through the effect."

"That said, becoming the subject of rumors isn't necessarily disadvantageous. The people we want to make aware of our existence aren't limited to our enemies."

"That means..."

At Russell's words, Subaru widened his eyes. The man quietly nodded toward him.

The people they wanted to attract with a conspicuous castle were undoubtedly their allies, with whom they currently had no way of getting in touch.

Aside from Emilia and the others, whose whereabouts were known, Rem and Otto, who had disappeared, as well as Roswaal and the others who had gone into hiding ahead of time, were all currently out of contact.

Even Subaru's group, despite acting alongside the 『Six Tongues』, had no means of communicating with their separated comrades.

However, if information about the floating castle spread, it would make it easier for those people to take action, for better or worse.

"Someone like Roswaal can fly here under his own power. He might even just hop aboard."

"To be honest, I cannot deny that we are hoping for precisely that. We are maintaining a considerable altitude, but Roswaal should be able to reach us without freezing."

"And if it's Roswaal, it wouldn't hurt if he froze a little, I suppose."

"Man, you're really tearing him apart, but honestly, he deserves it."

Roswaal was being thoroughly disparaged by two people who knew him particularly well, Russell and Beatrice. But since there was no denying that he had brought it upon himself, Subaru offered him no defense.

At any rate, the circumstances behind the castle taking flight, as well as the concerns about having done so, had more or less been resolved.

All that remained was—.

"If we've got a little time now, I'd like to explain what happened on our end. Also... Beako, do you have a room where we can let Lady Crusch rest?"

"There should be some guest rooms that haven't been ransacked. I'll show you the way, I suppose."

"Got it. Then Ferris should stay with us, so would it be okay to leave the report to Mel... I mean, 『White Sheep』 and 『Black Hound』? Once that's finished—"

"Yes, leave the report to me. —After that, let's talk."

Placing a hand against her chest, Melty nodded deeply. Her expression was quiet, but filled with resolve.

In her round eyes was a strong, sharp determination, as hard and brilliant as a diamond—completely at odds with her lovely and delicate appearance.

"—About what it is that I'm fighting for."

