"There is a place called Faradahl. That's where I come from... It was a remote region where members of the Evil Eye Tribe had lived for generations."

With an intentionally matter-of-fact voice, Melty began telling them her personal story.

This was after they had prepared the best guest room they could find in the castle and let Crusch rest there.

Leaving the sleeping Crusch in Ferris's care, Subaru and the others had chosen the second-best guest room as their meeting place. There, they listened to the story Melty had promised to tell them.

It was an important secret involving her, 『Black Hound』—and Tīga and Pūka.

"Speaking of the Evil Eye Tribe, I think there were a few of them in Vollachia. They're a demi-human race capable of using special powers, sort of like Divine Protections, right? Is that what you are too, Melty-chan?"

"Yes, that's correct. Faradahl was also a settlement on the outskirts of the Vollachian Empire, and I was one of the Evil Eye Tribe... I've already told you about the power of my Evil Eye, Subaru-san."

"Right. The 『Womanizer』 ability that makes people feel affection toward whoever you touch, right?"

Melty nodded seriously at Subaru's confirmation.

『Womanizer』—judging by the name alone, it didn't sound like a particularly serious power. However, throughout their activities with the 『Six Tongues』, Subaru had seen Russell rely on it time and time again.

In fact, she'd been chosen as one of the 『Beloved Children』. There was no doubt that her power was effective enough to warrant that.

As if to confirm that, Beatrice, who was holding Subaru's hand, murmured, "『Womanizer』..."

"I've heard of it, I suppose. Among the Evil Eyes created with the goal of reproducing the Authorities of the 『Witch』, it was supposed to be the 『Calamity Evil Eye』 that most closely achieved that objective."

"You know, for someone who's always being pretty and adorable right next to me, you sure occasionally drop some pretty explosive statements. What do you mean, reproducing the Authorities of the 『Witch』?"

"That was during the era of the 『Witch Wars』, so Betty doesn't have any firsthand experience with it. However, back then, 『Witches』 were springing up all over the place, and that was one of the countermeasures devised against them, I suppose. If you want to know more, I'll tell you another time. For now, concentrate on 『White Sheep』... on Melty's story."

"Damn it, I'm holding you to that promise...! Melty-chan, sorry for interrupting. Please continue."

"Yes. But just as the 『Librarian』 said, my power was known by that name. It was an effect that hadn't appeared in my family for hundreds of years, and everyone had regarded it as their long-cherished wish. ...I'm aware of just how frightening a power it is. But even that wasn't enough."

Before Subaru and Beatrice, Melty lowered her eyebrows and placed a hand against her chest.

With a strong sense of self-reproach and regret, she spoke of how it hadn't been enough. Then she let out a small breath.

"When I was little, I was careless about my own power, and because of that, I caused all sorts of conflicts. It was a terrible time. I deeply regret those things... But my real regret came shortly afterward."

"Regret... Could it be that you caught Capella's attention?"

"That's part of it, too. ...But my greatest regret isn't that."

"—"

"...It's Tīga."

After a brief moment of hesitation, Melty finally got to the heart of the matter.

Tīga Laureon—he was a member of the 『Divine Dragon Church』, Subaru's easygoing, like-minded friend with whom he'd hit it off, and an 『Executor』 said to be serving the enemy's 『Beloved Children』.

The extraordinary relationship between that Tīga and Melty was—.

"It was when both he and I were still children. A traveling troupe of performers came to Faradahl. Tīga was one of its members... I had been shunned by other people because I couldn't properly control my 『Womanizer』 ability, and I happened to meet Tīga. And then..."

"...And then?"

"—Using my 『Womanizer』 ability, I wished for him to stay by my side."

Clutching the front of her clothes tightly against her chest, Melty spoke as though confessing a sin.

She reiterated that she had been a small child at the time.

She had been born with an incomprehensibly tremendous power, and knew nothing about how to restrain it or use it properly. But Melty couldn't bring herself to excuse the mistakes caused by those circumstances simply because she had been a child.

"Tīga left behind the troupe, which had been like his family, and stayed in Faradahl. I was innocently happy about that... I dragged Tīga into this hell."

"Hell, I suppose? So that's what being one of the 『Beloved Children』 of the 『Archbishop of the Sin of Lust』 means."

"—Yes. In order to stay with me when Mama found me and took me away... In order to fulfill my 『request』, I don't know what conditions Tīga offered her. But to gain Mama's favor, how much of his own life did he have to sell off...!"

Her already pale skin turning deathly white, Melty's voice trembled weakly at the end.

The regret and remorse swirling inside her were conveyed to Subaru with painfully vivid clarity.

If Subaru's own mistakes had dragged someone precious to him—Emilia, Rem, Garfiel, Petra, or the others—into an inescapable hell, he would certainly regret it too.

"Didn't you take Betty and Otto into consideration, I suppose?"

"Well, you and Otto already gave me permission to drag you into hell..."

"I'm glad you understand. However, putting Otto on the same level as Betty is something I'll have to say a word or two to Otto about when we meet up again, I suppose."

Apparently, Beatrice had made some sort of decision in her mind.

After they reunited, Otto might have a few words for Subaru because of whatever Beatrice said to him. But, well, that was fine.

At any rate, Subaru now understood Melty's guilt toward Tīga and the bond between them.

He understood that much, but there was still something he didn't understand.

"I get that Tīga has such a deep connection with you, Melty-chan. But the way he acted when we encountered him beneath the castle was the exact opposite of what you've just described. That was..."

"—He doesn't remember me."

"—"

"Tīga has forgotten about me. ...No, it's not just Tīga. Mama, the other 『Beloved Children』, everyone in the world has forgotten me. —That's the reason I'm able to leave the 『Beloved Children』 now."

At Melty's answer, Beatrice slightly tightened her grip on Subaru's hand.

Understanding what she meant, Subaru also nodded.

Honestly, even before hearing this story, he'd already suspected that might be the case.

Considering the long and deep connection between Tīga and Melty that she'd just described, Subaru couldn't think of any other way their current interactions could have come about.

But if that was the case—.

"Those bastards from 『Gluttony』 didn't just horribly fracture the relationship between me and my Rem. They went and smeared mud all over Melty-chan's pure love too...!"

"It's not limited to Subaru and Rem, I suppose. There's Julius, the residents of Priestella... If we started counting everyone affected, we'd never finish."

"Even the matter of Roy being killed while in custody still has no identified culprit. They just keep scattering mysteries everywhere. Melty-chan managing to leave the 『Beloved Children』 isn't nearly enough to repay their debt."

To begin with, Capella, who had tormented Melty, was also an Archbishop of the Sin. It was practically a case of one Archbishop creating a problem and another Archbishop taking credit for solving it.

There was no merit to it whatsoever.

But while Subaru was getting angry about that, Melty's cheeks turned slightly red.

"U-Um, pure love is a bit..."

"Huh? It's not? But what happened between you and Tīga just now was completely—"

Subaru recalled the confrontation between Melty and Tīga beneath the castle.

The way she'd stared at Tīga when he appeared, stood in his path when he tried to flee, and then called out to him as he disappeared into the distance, her voice unable to reach him.

Every one of those actions had been the result of powerful affection.

That was what Subaru thought, and in response to his question, Melty spent a while stammering, "A-Aah..."

"P-Please, no comment... Besides, I..."

"—Hey, you know, this might be a bit of an old man's concern, but I think it's something I should say. If Melty-chan thinks that she doesn't deserve to love someone, or that she has no right to say Tīga is precious to her, then you're overthinking it. You don't need to think that way."

"H-How did you know!? Subaru-san, are you psychic...!?"

"I know it's a little strange for me to say this myself, but Subaru-san is pretty good at reading other people's situations when they're not his own."

"Really, it's strange for you to say that yourself..."

Brushing aside Beatrice's interjection from beside him, Subaru cleared his throat in front of the wide-eyed Melty.

There wasn't much advice Subaru could offer when it came to relationships between men and women. Even so, when someone was caught in an obviously fruitless internal struggle, he felt it was necessary to get to the root of the problem.

"I'm pretty knowledgeable when it comes to girls who think they don't deserve to be loved. After all, Emilia-tan, Rem, and Beako were all like that. ...Well, Beako's case was a little different, I guess? Better safe than sorry. Beako, I love you."

"Betty loves you too, I suppose. You don't need to say that right now."

"Taking courage from such an understanding Beako, I'll continue... Worrying about whether or not you deserve to be loved is pointless. Everyone deserves to be loved. The only exceptions are the Archbishops of the Sin."

"Subaru-san..."

"Like I said earlier, I'm not going to be charmed by you, Melty-chan. So if I think you're pretty, or that your voice is cute, that has nothing to do with your 『Womanizer』 ability."

"R-Really? You're not being charmed!?"

"I'm not, I'm not. Thinking someone's pretty and that I could stare at them forever is something I do with Ferris, too. I don't say it out loud because he'd probably give me a really nasty look. Beako, you're incredibly cute too. I could look at you forever."

"That's simply the result of Betty's charm, I suppose. It has nothing to do with the 『Womanizer』 ability."

As Subaru nodded and Beatrice proudly puffed out her chest, Melty looked back and forth between the two of them.

After blinking several times, she let out a soft breath.

It seemed as though she was finally exhaling some of the heavy feelings that had occupied her chest until just moments ago.

"You two are amazing..."

"Well, we've overcome quite a few trials as partners bound by fate."

"Indeed. We're veterans of countless battles, I suppose."

Subaru and Beatrice spoke proudly, as though the height and number of hurdles they'd overcome were on an entirely different level.

Of course, that didn't make Melty's hardships, suffering, or worries any less significant. Nor did it diminish what she'd experienced.

Whether their words could even serve as consolation was uncertain.

Even so, Melty wore a faint smile on her lips.

"I'll be sure to remember that. —That I might deserve to be loved, too."

It was an answer befitting a young girl who still lacked a little confidence.

However, giving her true confidence wasn't Subaru's job.

The man who needed to fulfill that role was currently among the enemy.

Still, Subaru now understood that there was a complicated but unbreakable history between Melty and Tīga.

But—.

"That brings me to something else. What exactly is the relationship between you and 『Black Hound』, Melty-chan? 『Black Hound』 also seems to have some sort of connection with that Great Spirit, Pūka. Since we're already on the subject, can we dig into that too?"

Taking advantage of the fact that Melty's account of her 『Womanizer』 ability had come to an end, Subaru ventured into something he'd been vaguely curious about but hadn't asked out of consideration for the atmosphere.

—『Black Hound』, who had left the 『Beloved Children』 alongside Melty and joined the 『Six Tongues』.

Despite all the nasty things he said, it was obvious that he cared about Melty. In the first place, 『Black Hound』 was foul-mouthed toward everyone, so the special treatment he showed Melty, visible in the moments when he wasn't being obnoxious, was undeniable.

However, once Tīga entered the picture, things became rather complicated.

"I don't know whose side I'm supposed to take: my friend Tīga or our current comrade, 『Black Hound』. Melty-chan, are you some kind of femme fatale?"

"S-Sinful!? So I really don't deserve to be loved after all...!"

"That was just a joke, don't take it seriously, I suppose. Subaru, don't go making Melty uncomfortable. You're a bad boy."

Because he'd said something unnecessary, Beatrice gave him a stern scolding.

But after taking a deep breath, Melty lowered her eyes and began.

"...Actually, I really don't know what my relationship with 『Black Hound』 is."

"Does that mean... you've forgotten 『Black Hound』, Melty-chan?"

"That's part of it, but... it seems that 『Black Hound』 himself doesn't know who he is either. As for his relationship with me, well, the only thing we know is that we've been together from the very beginning."

"Eh...? So it's not that 『Black Hound』 is hiding his relationship with you?"

"I don't think so. I don't think he's the kind of person who's that good at being deceptive..."

Her answer wasn't based on certainty so much as a strong desire to believe it.

Even so, Subaru agreed with Melty's assessment. 『Black Hound』 wasn't the sort of person who was good at playing mind games.

However, taking those things as their starting point brought an unnatural situation into focus.

"Everyone around him has forgotten him, and he's forgotten himself... That means..."

"Both his 『Name』 and 『Memories』 being devoured by the Authority of 『Gluttony』 would explain it, I suppose. But if both had been eaten, that would be impossible."

"Yeah... He should be in the same state as the 『Sleeping Beauty』."

If Melty's testimony was true, 『Black Hound』 should be in the same position as Rem, who had been attacked by 『Gluttony』 and fallen into a prolonged sleep.

He should be in the same condition as the people who still hadn't awakened in Priestella.

And yet, 『Black Hound』 hadn't fallen into a coma. He was walking around of his own free will.

Could it really be that, even now, they were discovering an entirely new form of victimhood caused by the Authority of 『Gluttony』?

"But if that's the case, then the relationship between 『Black Hound』 and Pūka makes sense too. In other words, those two were originally in a contractual relationship, but neither of them remembers it. That's why they're missing each other... It's the same situation as Julius and the spirits like Ia, whose contracts hadn't been undone, right?"

"That would be the explanation that makes the most sense, I suppose. ...But if that's the case, it's tragic."

"Tragic...?"

"For a spirit who chose someone as their contractor, there's nothing more painful than being forgotten by that contractor, I suppose."

"Ughhh! A sharp pain is slowly making its way toward me...! Beako, I'm sorry!!"

Picking Beatrice up, who slowly shook her head, Subaru desperately rubbed his cheek against hers.

From Beatrice's perspective, the period might have felt short, but it was nevertheless true that, for a time, Subaru had forgotten his contract with her because his 『Memories』 had been devoured.

But precisely because he understood that pain, Subaru was able to reconsider things.

"What's Tīga and Pūka's understanding of the situation right now? Originally, Tīga joined the 『Beloved Children』 because Melty-chan was there, right? But now Melty-chan isn't there anymore. The reason for his joining has been left hanging in midair."

"...I don't know. But I thought that Pūka had been searching for her contractor... for 『Black Hound』. If that's the case, then perhaps Tīga was also... That's what I hoped, but..."

"Melty-chan..."

With a helpless, bittersweet smile, Melty voiced the faint hope that had gone unfulfilled.

When she reunited with Tīga after being separated from him against her will, she'd held on to the slightest possibility that things might turn out differently.

But sadly, that hope hadn't come true.

That was the full extent of the tragic misunderstanding that had occurred beneath the castle.

"...Melty-chan, what do you want to do?"

Having accepted, digested, and understood the circumstances she was carrying, Subaru asked her that question.

Of course, Melty had left the 『Beloved Children』, joined the 『Six Tongues』, and resolved to thwart Capella's plans partly to secure her own safety and partly out of a sense of duty as someone who knew about the plan.

But now that he knew her circumstances, Subaru felt there had to be more to it than that.

—No, it wasn't that he merely thought so. He wanted there to be more.

Natsuki Subaru already liked Melty Pristis.

And Natsuki Subaru's way of doing things, despite being someone with plenty of affection to spare, was to want the people he loved to be as greedy as possible and to be happy.

And so—.

"If there's something you want to do, Melty-chan, I'll help you with anything."

"—Are you really not being charmed by me, Subaru-san?"

"Nope! There are plenty of people who hold the number-one spot in my heart...!"

"Subaru is always serious, I suppose. ...That's why things are difficult, and that's why you shouldn't put too much pressure on yourself either."

Still being held up for Subaru to rub his cheek against hers, Beatrice murmured with a sigh.

At her words, Melty caught her breath and whispered, "Ms. 『Librarian』..."

"You don't have to call me the 『Librarian』. Beatrice is fine. Betty will also stop calling you 『White Sheep』 and start calling you Melty, I suppose."

"Ahh... I feel like I'm the one who's going to end up being charmed by the two of you."

"Well, that means Beako's cuteness is on the level of an Evil Eye."

"Then Subaru's nasty-looking eyes are on the level of an Evil Eye, I suppose."

"That isn't a compliment, is it!? Aren't you just saying I have eyes like a demon!?"

"Ahaha."

At the misunderstanding of their compliments, Melty couldn't help covering her mouth and laughing.

She then let herself be carried along by the urge to laugh for a while. Eventually, after taking a deep breath, she spoke.

"—Subaru-san, Beatrice-san."

"Yeah."

"What is it, I suppose?"

Facing Melty, who had straightened her back and clasped her hands together in front of her stomach, Subaru and Beatrice waited.

The determination in her round eyes was unmistakable.

There were things that could be conveyed without words. Even so, important things needed to be put into words.

Just as one should tell someone precious that they love them, a determination to see something important through, no matter what, had to be proclaimed to the world.

And so—.

"—There is a life that I absolutely must take back. And in that life, there is someone I want by my side. Please lend me your strength so that I can get that person back."

"Yeah, I'd be happy to. Let's do this together. Our Lady Fate—"

"—Sounds good to me, I suppose."

Subaru and Beatrice thrust their fists forward.

Melty's eyes widened at the sight. Then, with a renewed expression of determination, she nodded and gently brought both her hands against their fists.

—It was a modest, yet unwavering declaration of resolve from Melty Pristis.
